      "artist": "Joshtesla",
      "description": "A model of Wardenclyffe Tower, the high voltage wireless station built by Nikola Tesla in 1901-1902. Designed as a transatlantic radiotelegraphy  and wireless power transmitter, it was never completed, and was torn down 1916.  A 187 ft wooden tower containing a Tesla coil oscillator, topped by a 68 ft diameter hemispherical metal capacitive electrode, in this model the shape of the top load has been changed to a toroidal shape.",
